---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../../layouts/main.astro';
import ProjectCollection from '../../components/ProjectCollection.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Projects"
  description="Explore Freddie Philpot's software projects: Markup, Dispatch, Waypoint, Glyph and a Linux home lab, with case studies and screenshots."
>
  <div class="wrap page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <h1>Projects</h1>
      <p>
        Applications and infrastructure projects, with source links,
        implementation decisions and validation notes.
      </p>
    </header>
    <section aria-label="Selected projects">
      <ProjectCollection />
    </section>
    <section class="case-section">
      <h2>Reading the case studies</h2>
      <div class="skill-rows">
        <div>
          <h3>What did I work on?</h3>
          <p>
            Each page describes the problem I wanted to solve and my work on the
            interface, configuration, implementation or testing. The source
            links provide more detail than the project cards. Dispatch’s build
            workflow, Glyph’s access checks and Waypoint’s session investigation
            are useful starting points for the technical decisions behind the
            interface.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Does a screenshot mean the app is production-ready?</h3>
          <p>
            A screenshot shows a particular interface state. It does not
            establish that authentication, delivery or recovery works in every
            environment. The case studies separate implemented features, local
            or simulator tests, production checks and remaining work. Sample
            records are identified in the captions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Where are the lessons and troubleshooting notes?</h3>
          <p>
            The <a href="/blog">writing section</a> covers individual questions,
            including DNS resolution and remote-access paths. The
            <a href="/projects/homelab">home-lab page</a> connects those notes
            to the services I run. Publication and update dates identify when
            the corresponding text was written or revised.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <div class="quiet-link">
      <a class="text-link" href="/projects/ctf">
        CTF write-ups
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
